<title>USA: Cleveland, Ohio, $81 mln issue pulled from market.</title>
<headline>Cleveland, Ohio, $81 mln issue pulled from market.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-08-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Technical problems have forced an $81 million Cleveland, Ohio, parking facilities revenue refunding bond issue, Series 1996, to be pulled from the market, according to Grigsby Branford &amp; Co, the offering's senior manager.</p>
<p>The issue had been priced and repriced on Thursday, August 22.</p>
<p>The firm said the issue will come to market again, but a sales date has not been specified.</p>
<p>--U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650</p>
